3. `worktrees/b1358-clone`, `-head`, `-base`, `-main`, `-probe`, `-merge`, `-scratch` or `session-tools/b1358` exists (`[ -e ]`, one path per call, BEFORE you create anything: round 1 created `session-tools/b1350` first and could not prove absence). **Pane:** `tmux display -p -t "$TMUX_PANE" '#{@cockpit_name}'` must read `Datasec/NexusAI-G362` (control `-t %0`); `tmux list-panes -a -F '#{@cockpit_name}' | awk -v me='Datasec/NexusAI-G362' '$0==me{c++} END{print c+0}'` must print 1. **Same-repository writer rule (test each REFUSE against the live seats; print each pane you excused, its `Yours` line with `/usr/bin/grep -n -i 'Yours'` (control: the N104 line prints and holds `backend/server.js`), and why):** `Datasec/NexusAI-N104` (kit `briefs/2026-11-06_B1340_SEAT-N104_nexusai-log-sinks-round2.md`, Yours `:126`: `backend/server.js`, three new `__tests__/rd79*|rd80*` files [the kit names `rd798`, `rd799`, `rd800`], at most one helper, the counts file, `worktrees/b1340-*`, `session-tools/b1340/`, jest tickets `b1340-build-*`) and `Datasec/NexusAI-N108` (kit `briefs/2026-11-06_B1354_SEAT-N108_nexusai-l2-tokens.md`, Yours `:138`: `scripts/derive-brand-tokens.js`, `static/css/tokens.css`, `docs/BRAND.md`, brand jest files, the counts file, `worktrees/b1354-*`, `session-tools/b1354/`, tickets `b1354-build-*`; its `:139` lists `tests/e2e/**` as NOT its own; its `:78` and `:100` mention this branch's four paths in READ-ONLY compare lines) are each excused only if the kit's `Yours:` names none of the four paths, `tests/e2e/` as a directory grant, `b1344b` nor `worktrees/b1358-*`; a mention in a Not-yours or compare-read line is not a grant. A pane whose kit you cannot find: `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY pane <name> has no kit`. The counts file is shared with N104, N108 and PR #178's lane; this branch does not touch it (say so). **A NexusAI pane that is running a build or a browser on one of the four files: STOP.**
4. `gh auth status` under the `GH_CONFIG_DIR` above not a Datasec account (say "the project account"; never quote the login). Lock or fence sha256 differing from FACTS: STOP with both values.
